 ## Overview
-The 2D Transfer Function Widget is an interactive visualization interface that presents a 2D slice of a multi-dimensional transfer function (TF) domain, allowing users to manually define and edit classification parameters while receiving real-time feedback from volume queries [S2]. It solves the problem of mapping spatial volume characteristics to optical properties by "re-projecting" local voxel data (values and derivatives) into the TF domain as graphical markers [S2]. Unlike standard point probes, it visualizes the local gradient and curvature structure by connecting corner points with edges reflecting spatial connectivity, enabling users to distinguish between homogeneous regions and boundaries [S1, unofficial][S2]. It builds on [Interaction and Editing Interfaces](6592-interaction-and-editing-interfaces.md) by providing a direct-manipulation canvas for the TF definition.
+The 2D Transfer Function Widget is an interactive visualization interface that presents a 2D slice of a multi-dimensional transfer function (TF) domain, allowing users to manually define and edit classification parameters while receiving real-time feedback from volume queries [S2]. It solves the problem of mapping spatial volume characteristics to optical properties by "re-projecting" local voxel data (values and derivatives) into the TF domain as graphical markers [S2]. Unlike standard point probes, it visualizes the local gradient and curvature structure by connecting corner points with edges reflecting spatial connectivity, enabling users to distinguish between homogeneous regions and boundaries [S2]. It builds on [Interaction and Editing Interfaces](6592-interaction-and-editing-interfaces.md) by providing a direct-manipulation canvas for the TF definition [G].
 
